From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KeinNiemand <18308201+KeinNiemand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 14:50:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] btrfs: honor allocator hints for fixed-width mirrors

gather_device_info() admits complete allocation-hint groups until it
has at least devs_min devices. It then clears the hints and sorts the
admitted devices globally by max_avail. For a fixed-width mirrored
profile, that second sort can move preferred devices past the later
devs_max cutoff.

RAID1, RAID1C3 and RAID1C4 currently use exactly devs_min devices.
Limit the hint-ordered prefix to that fixed count before clearing the
hints. Devices within each hint group are already ordered by max_avail,
so this keeps the best devices needed from the final group.
The existing second sort then restores the max_avail ordering expected
by stripe-size calculation over the selected devices only.

Check that devs_min and devs_max match instead of relying on the
current RAID1 profile definitions implicitly. If a future RAID1 profile
becomes variable-width, it will retain the existing whole-group
behavior.

Leave all other profiles unchanged, in particular the wide striped
profiles that need the complete final candidate group.

A preferred device remains eligible while it has at least
dev_extent_min free. It can therefore constrain stripe_size and produce
a small block group. This behavior already exists when the preferred
tier alone satisfies the profile; this change intentionally extends it
to fixed-width mirrors assembled from multiple hint tiers.

v2:
- Document the possible chunk-size constraint from a nearly full
  preferred device.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: KeinNiemand <18308201+KeinNiemand@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
---
 fs/btrfs/volumes.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/btrfs/volumes.c b/fs/btrfs/volumes.c
index 14bea7d037c3d..291dc31ff306b 100644
--- a/fs/btrfs/volumes.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/volumes.c
@@ -6030,6 +6030,19 @@ static int gather_device_info(struct btrfs_fs_devices *fs_devices,
 			break;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Fixed-width mirrored profiles consume only the first devs_max
+	 * candidates. Keep the highest-priority devices and only as many of
+	 * the final hint group as needed. The sort below then restores the
+	 * max_avail ordering required by the stripe-size calculation.
+	 *
+	 * Check the fixed-width property explicitly so a future variable-width
+	 * RAID1 profile retains the existing whole-group behavior.
+	 */
+	if ((ctl->type & BTRFS_BLOCK_GROUP_RAID1_MASK) &&
+	    ctl->devs_min == ctl->devs_max)
+		ndevs = min(ndevs, ctl->devs_max);
+
 	BUG_ON(ndevs > ctl->ndevs);
 	ctl->ndevs = ndevs;
 
